resize-amdgpu-bars (1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Unit: enable SystemCallFilter=@system-service @module @raw-io with
    SystemCallErrorNumber=EPERM (validated on real hardware).
  * Read-only commands no longer write the runtime state directory.
  * Reject a configuration that cannot finish inside the unit's
    TimeoutStartSec; document the rule in resize-amdgpu-bars.conf(5).
  * Journal cosmetics: "none" for empty BAR lists; ROCm tools named only
    when installed.
  * /var/log/resize-amdgpu-bars is package-owned and removed on purge.
  * Style checks and shellcheck -S style enforced by the build.

 -- Exabit Networks <packages@exabit.io>  Thu, 03 Sep 2026 02:55:00 +0000

resize-amdgpu-bars (1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial public release. Resizable BAR for AMD GPUs behind PCIe
    switches: programs the BAR size, re-enumerates only the all-GPU PCI
    subtrees on their own root bus so the kernel re-sizes the bridge windows,
    and loads amdgpu once behind a bind guard. The upstream changelog
    (changelog.gz in the package documentation) records the internal builds.

 -- Exabit Networks <packages@exabit.io>  Thu, 03 Sep 2026 01:01:10 +0000
